- op: discuss  # 1236
  at: '2026-06-02T08:02:26Z'  # 1236
  by: agent  # 1236
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1236
  clock: 6  # 1236
  nonce: '1236'  # 1236
  message: "Pass-32 face: post-INV-sugat substrate confirms WI-vusaf's existing repro list + adds `--max-symbols 99999` runaway (F32.10).\n\nWI-vusaf's existing description (2026-05-28 baseline) lists three repros: `--max-symbols 50 --min-symbols 100` (silent), `--coverage 1.5` (silent), `--coverage -0.5` (silent), `--max-symbols 0` (clamp-to-1). Pass-32 re-ran the same flag matrix on the post-INV-sugat-closure substrate (`/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json`); all five WI-vusaf cases still reproduce, and the substrate is unchanged from 2026-05-28 in terms of validator behavior:\n\n```\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --coverage -0.5 --out ... → exit 0\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --coverage  1.5 --out ... → exit 0\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --coverage  2.0 --out ... → exit 0\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --coverage banana --out ... → exit 2 (argparse float-parse)\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --max-symbols -1 --out ... → exit 0\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --max-symbols  0 --out ... → exit 0\n$ hypergumbo compact --input bm.json --max-symbols 99999 --out ... → TIMEOUT at 30s (no exit)\n```\n\nThe last row is the new face: **`--max-symbols` accepts values larger than the substrate's node count (34253) and proceeds to run without a clamp-to-available optimization, exceeding 30 seconds**. The default compact run completes in 4 seconds; raising the budget by 1000× yields >30s wall-clock with no progress indication. No upper bound check.\n\n**Why pass-32 is filing this.** Cumulative: the silent acceptance of `--coverage` out-of-range is the spec issue (range is documented as 0.0–1.0); the `--max-symbols 99999` runaway is a new symptom that argues for **range AND upper-bound discipline together** — not just rejecting negatives and >1 ratios, but also clamping or rejecting requests larger than the substrate's actual size. INV-pazur tile already documents the `nodes_summary` post-shrink reconciliation gap; pass-32 supplies the input-validation symmetric face: the budget can be set so high that the shrink loop becomes a no-op but the wall-clock blows out.\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** The argparse-action factory from INV-dunof's \"Fix shape\" should bound `--max-symbols` to `[1, len(bm.nodes)]` when `--input` is provided (the input file is already loaded and counted by the time argparse finishes; the bound is cheap to compute). For `--coverage`, bound to `[0.0, 1.0]` with a clear argparse error message. The compact-50 ⊄ compact-200 monotonicity face (filed against INV-fanur) is a separate concern downstream of the budget-acceptance gate.\n\n**No status change.** WI-vusaf's existing scope already covers the 5 silent-accept faces; pass-32 supplies the post-substrate confirmation and the 99999-runaway extension. Probe artifact: `/tmp/p32_outputD.log` section \"D.10\"."  # 1236
