  message: "Fixed + merged (selfh/dev c4f87c6a77, bundled with WI-pizat). compact now rejects numerically invalid flags at the argparse boundary (exit 2): --max-symbols<1, --min-symbols<0, --coverage outside [0,1] via reusable _positive_int_arg/_nonneg_int_arg/_unit_interval_arg factories (also wired onto run --coverage, structural analogue), plus a cross-flag max<min guard in cmd_compact. 0.0/1.0 coverage stay valid. Behavioral evidence: validator unit tests + main() SystemExit(2) tests for each bad value + a cross-flag rc=2 test; existing cmd_compact tests (coherent values) stay green; core 100%. cli-input-validation sub-B (INV-dunof); the shared factories are reusable for INV-jibof/INV-fapid/INV-votop. Wave-4 projection."  # adba
